  "description": "Does contract-term extraction hold up on long, scanned document packets whose amendments have to be sorted out? 60 synthetic packets of 7,000–20,000 words (an agreement with the graded articles in its back half, five schedules, 4–16 SOWs with their own terms, caps and laws as distractors) at three scan-noise levels; 44 carry a trap: amendment chains filed out of order, a restatement that supersedes an earlier amendment, unsigned, one-party and future-effective amendments, renewal and term changes, and clauses that are simply absent. Extract eight terms as they stand on the status date.",
